# The native shell's build artefacts (issue #36).
#
# Scoped to this directory on purpose. The repo root's .gitignore describes a
# no-build static site and should keep describing one.

# Capacitor's dependencies. The reason this whole directory exists is to keep
# these out of the repo root.
node_modules/

# THE webDir. Generated by ../tools/mobile/prepare-webdir.mjs on every build,
# and it is a COPY of index.html / app.js / styles.css / player/ / the runtime
# data subset. Committing it would create the second copy of the player that the
# prepare script's header exists to prevent: the site would get a fix and the
# committed copy would not.
www/

# ── The generated native projects: BOTH IGNORED IN FULL ──────────────────────
#
# This block used to say the opposite — that `mobile/ios/` and `mobile/android/`
# are NOT ignored, because Capacitor's own guidance is to commit them. Both
# platforms have since been generated, and the practice the repo actually settled
# on is the other one, so the rule now matches it. Written down rather than
# quietly flipped, because the old argument was not silly.
#
# WHAT SETTLED IT — the same call, twice, independently:
#   - iOS. PR #213 (on #220) builds the shell on a macOS runner by running
#     `npm run add:ios` in the job and building what it generates. `mobile/ios/`
#     is not in the repo and the workflow does not want it to be.
#   - Android. Issue #37 built `mobile/android/` on Windows and got both APKs
#     (`docs/android-shell-build.md`). Committing it was rejected for the same
#     reason: ~100 generated files, no reviewer, and this directory AUTO-MERGES
#     with no post-merge review window.
#
# So the generate step must be reproducible from `mobile/package.json` alone, and
# it is: `npm install && npm run add:android` (or `add:ios`) needs nothing that is
# not committed. `capacitor.config.json` — the only file that carries a DECISION
# (the app id, the platform paths) — is committed, and is pinned by
# `tools/mobile/shell-invariants.test.mjs`.
#
# THE ONE THING THIS COSTS, stated plainly because it is a real loss. The Android
# `res/xml/config.xml` was deliberately left un-ignored so the `KeepRunning`
# footgun could be parsed by a test — an ignored file cannot be checked. Ignoring
# the platform means CI never sees that file. The vector it defended against goes
# away with it: `KeepRunning="false"` can no longer be committed, because the file
# it would live in can no longer be committed. `cap add` regenerates it from
# Capacitor's template on every machine, and the template sets no preference at
# all. The guard is now a check on the machine that generated the platform —
# which is the machine that builds the APK, so it still runs where it matters.
# The committed half of that guard (the parsed `capacitor.config.json`, at any
# depth, case-insensitively) is untouched and still runs in CI.
#
# ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, and that is not cosmetic. These lines used to read
# `ios/` and `android/`, and a gitignore pattern with no leading slash matches a
# directory of that name AT ANY DEPTH. So `android/` silently ignored
# `plugins/foray-audio/android/` — this repo's OWN hand-written foreground-service
# code — and `git add mobile/plugins` staged the package.json and the web half while
# dropping every .java file, the build.gradle and the manifest without a word.
# Caught by noticing four files missing from `git status`, which is luckier than it
# should have been: a reviewer would have seen a plugin with no native code in it and
# the Android build on the generating machine would still have passed, because the
# untracked files were right there on disk.
#
# What these two lines were ever meant to ignore is the GENERATED PLATFORM, which is
# `mobile/android/` and `mobile/ios/` exactly — `capacitor.config.json` says so, and
# `shell-invariants.test.mjs` reads those paths out of it. Anchoring says that and
# nothing more. Native code we WRITE lives under `plugins/` and is committed; see
# docs/android-native-code.md.
/ios/
/android/

# ── If you ever un-ignore a platform above, YOU NEED THE RULES BELOW TOO ──────
#
# An earlier draft of this file deleted every per-platform output rule and left a
# comment claiming they were "kept for anyone who un-ignores a platform above".
# They were not, and a reviewer measured the cost: **2,569 of the 2,623 files under
# `mobile/android/` were covered by nothing except the blanket `android/` line.**
# Deleting that one line would have staged all of them — including
# `local.properties`, which carries a machine-absolute `sdk.dir`, and
# `app/src/main/assets/public/`, which is the duplicate copy of the player that the
# `www/` rule above exists to prevent.
#
# So the output rules are restored and kept beside the blanket ignore. They are
# redundant while the blanket rules stand, and they are what makes un-ignoring a
# platform a safe, single-line edit instead of a 2,500-file accident.
#
# MEASURED, both ways, on a generated Android project (2,623 files):
#   - with only the blanket `android/` line, commenting it out exposes 2,621 files,
#     including `local.properties` and `app/src/main/assets/public/`;
#   - with the rules below in place, commenting it out exposes **53** — the real
#     project files someone doing that would actually mean to commit — and
#     `local.properties` and `assets/public/` are NOT among them.

# iOS
ios/App/App/public/
ios/App/App/capacitor.config.json
ios/App/Pods/
ios/App/output/
ios/App/build/
ios/App/App.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/
ios/App/App.xcodeproj/xcuserdata/
ios/capacitor-cordova-ios-plugins/
*.xcuserstate
DerivedData/

# ── Our OWN plugins' Gradle build output ──────────────────────────────────────
#
# `mobile/plugins/*/android/` is a real Gradle library module (docs/android-native-code.md),
# so Gradle writes a `build/` tree into it exactly as it does for the generated app.
# None of the `android/…` rules below cover it: a gitignore pattern containing a
# slash is anchored to THIS directory, so `android/build/` means `mobile/android/build/`
# and nothing else.
#
# FOUND BY A FAILURE, not by foresight. `git add -A` tried to stage this tree and
# died with *"Filename too long"* on
# `plugins/foray-audio/android/build/.transforms/<hash>/transformed/bundleLibRuntimeToDirRelease/…/PlaybackKeepAliveService.dex`.
# A shorter hash would have committed several hundred build artefacts into a
# directory that AUTO-MERGES with no post-merge review window. `shell-invariants.test.mjs`
# now asserts this is ignored, in the same test that asserts the plugin's SOURCES
# are not.
plugins/*/android/build/
plugins/*/android/.gradle/
plugins/*/android/.cxx/
plugins/*/android/local.properties

# Android
android/.gradle/
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/app/src/main/assets/public/
android/app/src/main/assets/capacitor.config.json
android/app/src/main/assets/capacitor.plugins.json
android/app/src/main/res/xml/config.xml
android/capacitor-cordova-android-plugins/
android/local.properties
android/.idea/
*.iml
*.apk
*.aab
